{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1452779-what-you-need-to-know-about-spirits-fluff-wise","id":1452779,"title":"What you need to know about Spirits. (Fluff wise)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-18T08:13:37-07:00","id":1452779,"title":"What you need to know about Spirits. (Fluff wise)","content":"I created this video to go over how Spirits behave and what types of Spirits there are in Chronicles of Darkness. I mostly go over the Spirits portrayed in Werewolf the Forsaken, but still should be informative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MK1gH2qJ6o0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MK1gH2qJ6o0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/MK1gH2qJ6o0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/MK1gH2qJ6o0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>This video covers:</b><ul><li>Muthra</li> <li>Hursihim</li> <li>Ensihim</li> <li>Dihim</li> <li>Ilusahim</li> <li>Lunes</li> <li>Helions</li> <li>Magath</li> <li>Possessed</li> <li>Claimed</li> <li>Spirit Thieves</li> <li>Hosts</li> <li>Spider-Hosts</li> <li>Rat-Hosts</li> <li>Idigam</li> <li>Forge Servants</li> </ul><br /> <b>In case you don't know Werewolf the Forsaken's terminology:</b><ul><li>5 Basic Spirits types</li> <li>Moon Spirits</li> <li>Sun Spirits</li> <li>Hybrid Spirits</li> <li>Possessed</li> <li>Hybrid Organic/Spirits</li> <li>Shards of Spirit Gods</li> <li>Alien Spirits</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T12:10:11-07:00","id":1452809,"title":"","content":"Personally, I really dislike threads that are meant to be informative and then just link to a Youtube video.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T13:17:29-07:00","id":1452813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1452779-what-you-need-to-know-about-spirits-fluff-wise?p=1452809#post1452809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I really dislike threads that are meant to be informative and then just link to a Youtube video.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a problem with creating YouTube videos in this regard. Mainly that no one sees them unless you share them, viewers share them, or the YouTube algorithm deems them profitable enough to send to people's homepages.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for non-video content. Here is my entire script for this video and you can read at your own speed:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What is a Spirit in Chronicles of Darkness?</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirits are sentient representations of concepts within the real world. For example, a spirit of wisdom or spirit of trees. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What a Spirit is not is a ghost or an angel. I will cover those later.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Chronicles of Darkness, Spirits typically reside in the Spirit world also known as the Shadow or Hisil. The Shadow is a parallel reality that mirrors our reality. There is an invisible barrier between our world and the Shadow called the Gauntlet. Places where the Gauntlet is thinnest allows Spirits from the Shadow to reach across and affect our world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Where do spirits come from?</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirits are typically created in the Shadow when something new is created in the real world and generates the resource called essence. Tell a brand new joke, you might just have created a joy or humor spirit. Build a new computer, then you may have created a computer spirit. These newly formed spirits are equivalent to seeds or eggs, created but not quite done yet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note when I call a Spirit a spirit of joy or technology that term is what they resonate with. A spirit of Joy for instance will typically feed on Essence created from Joy, Happiness, or similar emotions. If it fed off of the polar opposite of its resonance such as sadness or despair it can mutate into a dangerous hybrid creature that I\u2019ll talk about later on in the Spirit Types section.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As this newly formed spirit is exposed to more and more essence similar to the type that created it, it will eventually awaken as a pretty simple spirit. The equivalent of an animal. As the Spirit feeds on other Spirits and essence that match its resonance it will grow in complexity and power until it becomes a conscious entity. As it mixes and matches essence types of similar resonances it will differ drastically from its original form. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So Spirits of the same type in two different locations will likely be different because they may feed off of different resonate essence types. For example a spirit of trees in the city may feed on the spirits of wooden structures, while a spirit of trees in a forest might feed off of bird spirits that get too close.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit Politics</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every spirit is categorized into an Umia, which is a broad collection or category. Similar to how animals are classified as mammals, reptiles, etc\u2026 In this case, categories such as weather, animals, fungi, vehicles, emotions, etc...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Umia is what Spirits are born into, but then there are Ilthum which are communities of spirits that they can join. For instance, a Spirit of Tools may choose to join an Ithum of Spirits of Knives or Hammers. Or a spirit of fire choosing between lava or candle flame Ilthums.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When a single Spirit rules over a region, sentient Spirits within that location are called a Court.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When Spirits form a small group under a common purpose that is called a Brood. The werewolf the forsaken book compares this to Werewolf packs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirits have their own feudal system, kind of. The lower sentient spirits give essence to the more powerful ones as a tax. If a spirit pays this tax they are protected, if they don\u2019t they might be killed by other spirits. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It should be noted that Spirits cannot accept a deal until they are paid. So make sure you have your payment at the ready. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit Ranks</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirits come in many shapes and sizes, but most are ranked by how powerful they are. Your typical spirit falls under the following ranking system.</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Muthra are freshly formed spirits that lay dormant in the Spirit world. Other Spirits eat these the same way a human might eat fruit or eggs.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hursihim are active spirits that act on instinct more than thought and are bound to a specific location or object. Hursihim are commonly recruited by Werewolf packs as a pack Totem Spirit.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ensihim are sentient spirits that no longer run on instinct and can feed from more than one type of Essence. It is at this point that they can join the local Spirit court. These make up the majority of Spirits that escape into the mundane world as well.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dihim are potent spirits that can feed off of a wide range of Essence types. They are so powerful that their presence can manipulate the landscape of the Shadow, such as creating areas saturated with fear or that look futuristic. Dihim are the most powerful Spirits that can crossover into the mundane world and are extremely dangerous when they do so.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ilusahim are indistinguishable from gods. They encompass global or universal concepts such as the Sun and Moon. Their lairs are hidden deep inside the Shadow in areas that are extremely hard to reach. Ilusahim are so powerful that they are unable to cross the Gauntlet into the Mundane World as reality cannot support their power.</span></span></li> </ol><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other Types of Spirits</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirits are a wide category, but there are other things that fall under the category of Spirits that aren\u2019t considered your default spirits. So I\u2019ll try to go over them as quickly as possible. Note that each one of these could be its own video.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lunes are Spirits of the Moon who act as emissaries to Earth for their patron, Luna. Luna is the mother of Werewolves and as such Lunes are known for helping Werewolves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Helions are Spirits of the Sun who act as emissaries to Earth for their patron Helios. Because werewolves killed Luna\u2019s lover, Father Wolf, Helios and his Helions are very hostile towards Werewolves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Remember those dangerous hybrids I mentioned earlier, Magath are spirits that have fed from conflicting concepts, such as a spirit of fire devouring a spirit of water. These Spirits are ostracized by the Spirit courts because of their hybrid nature. A Magath often continues devouring more conflicting spirits to continue evolving their chaotic form.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hosts</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hosts are fragments of Spirit Gods that were shattered by the Spirit God, Father Wolf. These shards appear as swarms that burrow into human flesh and incubate inside them. Hoping one day to piece themselves back together into one entity. If you kill a person infected by Hosts the corpse will erupt into a swarm of creatures, kill every single one because if even one escapes it can infect someone else and multiply.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hosts have a detrimental effect on the Gauntlet. Azlu are the Spider Hosts and they create webs that reinforce the Gauntlet, making Spirits unable to cross or get Essence from the mundane world. Beshilu are the Rat Hosts they gnaw at the gauntlet allowing for Spirits to more easily cross into the mundane world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Others do exist, but you are encouraged to make your own.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit Ridden</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Urged are humans that have a spirit following them. The Spirit can influence the human\u2019s decisions to generate Essence to sustain itself. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Claimed are what happens when a Spirit possesses a living being so much that the Spirit and flesh merge into one being. The Spirit mutates its host until it transforms them into an amalgamation of Spirit and Flesh. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit Thieves are what happens when a Spirit quickens the Claiming process to the point that it suppresses the host-body\u2019s consciousness. Often this is done when a Spirit is running away from something.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Idigam</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Idigam are spirits of Chaos whose origin is hotly debated by werewolves. What is known is that they arrived soon after the Apollo Moon Landing missions. Fun fact there have been six moon landings and twelve people have walked on the moon. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not so fun fact, Idigam come in two forms: the formless in which they are constantly changing form and function, and then finally the Coalescing when Earth\u2019s reality forces it to stay in one form. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also Idigam have the power to manipulate anything related to Essence. They can manipulate Spirits, the Gauntlet, the Shadow, Ghosts, and Loci that bridge the mundane world and the Shadow. They can also remove souls from people and werewolves to turn them into Forge Servants which are the Idigam version of Claimed called Forge Claimed and Empty Wolves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Idigam can also transform Spirits into beings of flesh called Flesh Spirits. Essentially Spirits which are always manifested and cannot become incorporeal or go into the Shadow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forge Heralds are willing human or werewolf servants to the idigam. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And Forge Spawn are lesser versions of the original Idigam.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ve got to say, Idigam scare me more than any other antagonist in this book.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","user":"DontEatRawHagis","date":". 06-18-2021, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T06:22:44-07:00","id":1452944,"title":"","content":"I feel like I've been hit with an occult dictionary. xD<br /> <br /> I feel this topic should be drilled into depth-wise, step-by-step, rather than with broad sweeps. I feel that all the spirit-antagonists such as Idigam, the Hosts, etc... are not part of the core concept of understanding spirits, so could be left out in a &quot;spirits 101&quot; video. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other Types of Spirits&quot; too, and you essentially said as much yourself.<br /> <br /> All of the specific terms could have been toned down a bit as well. Simply knowing what the progression of spirits is like is enough, don't really need the Werewolf terms for this. As it's posted in the general CoFD forum, I imagine it's meant to be generally useful to everyone and not aimed specifically at Werewolf; no point for me to know the name &quot;Hursihim&quot; for my Changeling game. ^^</span></span><br /> <br /> To replace all this content, I'd have enjoyed more examples and deeper look into what Spirits actually <i>are</i> and <i>do</i> more. The small note about how two different spirits of trees might act is great. But I don't actually see in what way a spirit that feeds off of wooden structures would actually be different from a spirit that eats bird spirits while hanging around in a tree. And the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ilthums I understand even less; surely a spirit of fire has an origin such as lava or candles or hearthfire, so why wouldn't it simply choose an Ilthum related to its origin, and how does choosing one affect it when it happens... ? What do Ilthums do, and is it likely to be relevant for a non-werewolf chronicle?<br /> <br /> I don't really feel I can incorporate spirits into my Chronicle better after this video, and I think that should be the main goal. ^^</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T07:47:26-07:00","id":1453162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1452779-what-you-need-to-know-about-spirits-fluff-wise?p=1452944#post1452944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I've been hit with an occult dictionary. xD<br /> <br /> I feel this topic should be drilled into depth-wise, step-by-step, rather than with broad sweeps. I feel that all the spirit-antagonists such as Idigam, the Hosts, etc... are not part of the core concept of understanding spirits, so could be left out in a &quot;spirits 101&quot; video. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other Types of Spirits&quot; too, and you essentially said as much yourself.<br /> <br /> All of the specific terms could have been toned down a bit as well. Simply knowing what the progression of spirits is like is enough, don't really need the Werewolf terms for this. As it's posted in the general CoFD forum, I imagine it's meant to be generally useful to everyone and not aimed specifically at Werewolf; no point for me to know the name &quot;Hursihim&quot; for my Changeling game. ^^</span></span><br /> <br /> To replace all this content, I'd have enjoyed more examples and deeper look into what Spirits actually <i>are</i> and <i>do</i> more. The small note about how two different spirits of trees might act is great. But I don't actually see in what way a spirit that feeds off of wooden structures would actually be different from a spirit that eats bird spirits while hanging around in a tree. And the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ilthums I understand even less; surely a spirit of fire has an origin such as lava or candles or hearthfire, so why wouldn't it simply choose an Ilthum related to its origin, and how does choosing one affect it when it happens... ? What do Ilthums do, and is it likely to be relevant for a non-werewolf chronicle?<br /> <br /> I don't really feel I can incorporate spirits into my Chronicle better after this video, and I think that should be the main goal. ^^</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This post has been lingering with me in regards to my next video on the mechanics of Spirits. Its making me rethink how I organize my next video.<br /> <br /> Now I won't be using any First Tongue(Spirit/Werewolf language) terminology aside from Idigam. But It is kind of hard when you talk about the Spirit Courts as these terms are how Spirits refer to one another. I do understand that this can be very overwhelming for those unfamiliar. I'm hoping that at the very least its easier to navigate than the books.<br /> <br /> Originally I was going to section off the video to follow an outline like this, but now am thinking to remove the Hosts and Idigam from the video and put them into their own, what do you think? This is still a lot of ground to cover, but the mechanics are pretty dense in their own way:<ul><li>Places where Spirits are found:<ul><li>Material World</li> <li>Twilight</li> <li>Gauntlet (Barrier between Material and Shadow)</li> <li>Shadow</li> </ul></li> <li>Spirit Forms and Manifestations<ul><li>Twilight Form</li> <li>Discorporate</li> <li>Reaching</li> <li>Gauntlet Breach</li> <li>Shadow Gateway</li> <li>Image</li> <li>Materialize</li> <li>Fetter/Unfetter</li> <li>Possess</li> <li>Claim</li> </ul></li> <li>Spirit Influence Abilities<ul><li>Strengthen</li> <li>Manipulate</li> <li>Control</li> <li>Create</li> <li>Mass Create</li> </ul></li> <li>Spirit Numina<ul><li>Normal Numina</li> <li>Reach Numina</li> </ul></li> <li>Spirit Ridden Mechanics<ul><li>Urged qualities</li> <li>Possessed qualities</li> <li>Claimed qualities<ul><li>Dread powers</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Hosts<ul><li>Host qualities</li> <li>Spider-Host Dread Powers</li> <li>Rat-Host Dread Powers</li> </ul></li> <li>Idigam<ul><li>Formless qualities</li> <li>Coalescing qualities</li> <li>Essence Shaping</li> <li>Dread Powers</li> <li>Forge Servants<ul><li>Forge Claimed</li> <li>Forge Empty Wolf</li> <li>Forge Flesh-Bound Spirit</li> <li>Forge Herald</li> <li>Forge Spawn</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T08:51:02-07:00","id":1453170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1452779-what-you-need-to-know-about-spirits-fluff-wise?p=1453162#post1453162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Places where Spirits are found:<ul><li>Material World</li> <li>Twilight</li> <li><b>Gauntlet (Barrier between Material and Shadow)</b></li> <li>Shadow</li> </ul></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Not generally. Something funky (probably involving Hosts) needs to happen for spirits to end up <b>inside</b> the Gauntlet. (There are entities within the Gauntlet according to a first edition Mage book, but it also says they're not quite spirits.)<br /> <br /> Also, Twilight is a state of being and not a place (unless you're playing Mummy, but that's the wrong Twilight and not relevant here). Spirits in the Material World are always in Twilight unless they have physical bodies (aka Materalized or Claimed).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Spirit Forms and Manifestations<ul><li>Twilight Form</li> <li>Discorporate</li> <li>Reaching</li> <li>Gauntlet Breach</li> <li>Shadow Gateway</li> <li>Image</li> <li>Materialize</li> <li>Fetter/Unfetter</li> <li>Possess</li> <li>Claim</li> </ul></li> <li>Spirit Influence Abilities<ul><li>Strengthen</li> <li>Manipulate</li> <li>Control</li> <li>Create</li> <li>Mass Create</li> </ul></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>These are definitely the mechanically most important to explain. I would start with Influences because they're both more core to a spirit's nature and are often used to facilitate Manifestations. Just don't forget that Manifestation Conditions can be applied without Influences.<br /> Unfortunately Influences are so underexplained in what they can do even veterans of the game have trouble using them without just glossing over the actual rules and just have them do whatever they think is fitting for the current scene and the spirit's power level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Hosts</li> <li>Idigam</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>I would definitely skip these. Hosts aren't spirits. Their relevance is just how they affect the local spirit ecology, which doesn't seem to be relevant in a video about rules for spirits.<br /> Idigam, while much closer to being spirits, are still way too different and also too rare for it to be worth describing them in a video about spirits in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T18:48:14-07:00","id":1456848,"title":"","content":"For a general talk about spirits you should definitely refrain from using First Language (A.K.A. fake Sumerian) and referencing Werewolf so much. Either keep to &quot;neutral&quot; information or include positions from other splats, no matter how fringe a member with contact with spirits would be.<br /> <br /> This is specially true for spirits among all the &quot;Twilight Denizens&quot; because they're the ones with more frequent and broad contact with the Material, given how they are shaped but also shape Essence across the Gauntlet. Everything else is too localized in comparison, spirits theoretically are a thing to everyone everywhere even if those people don't perceive it (the truth is that most people do perceive it in some level and have some grasp of the concept even if they can't actually see or touch spirits directly).<br /> <br /> About the language, despite it being the language of the spirits themselves, it should go on its own video. The purpose of this one was to explain spirits to humans, not to &quot;spirit children&quot;, and the language just got in the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}